From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:33:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] libavfilter: add the gsc_v4l2m2m filter for the Exynos
 GScaler

The display mixer on Exynos 5422 (ODROID-XU4) only has RGB planes, so
the YUV frames from the MFC decoder cannot be shown with direct to
plane rendering. Its planes cannot scale either (only 1:1 or 2x).

The gsc_v4l2m2m filter imports DRM PRIME frames (NV12, NV21 or YUV420,
in one or more objects) into the GScaler as dmabufs and returns
XRGB8888 DRM PRIME frames. No CPU copy is involved. An input frame is
released only after its conversion has finished.

Without options, the whole pitch is converted, so no cropping is
needed; the frames keep the visible size. With the w and h options,
the visible area is scaled to that size (e.g. the display size) and the
frames have square pixels.

The conversion of one frame overlaps with the decoding of the next
one, so frames come out one frame later. The "flush" command drops the
frames in the converter, so that the filter can be kept on seek.

Based on the decoder->converter pipeline by memeka:
https://github.com/mihailescu2m/FFmpeg/commits/v4l2-drmprime
---
 libavfilter/Makefile         |   1 +
 libavfilter/allfilters.c     |   1 +
 libavfilter/vf_gsc_v4l2m2m.c | 862 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 864 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libavfilter/vf_gsc_v4l2m2m.c

diff --git a/libavfilter/Makefile b/libavfilter/Makefile
index c09dd54..1ae47a5 100644
--- a/libavfilter/Makefile
+++ b/libavfilter/Makefile
@@ -339,6 +339,7 @@ OBJS-$(CONFIG_GRADFUN_FILTER)                += vf_gradfun.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_GRAPHMONITOR_FILTER)           += f_graphmonitor.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_GRAYWORLD_FILTER)              += vf_grayworld.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_GREYEDGE_FILTER)               += vf_colorconstancy.o
+OBJS-$(CONFIG_GSC_V4L2M2M_FILTER)            += vf_gsc_v4l2m2m.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_GUIDED_FILTER)                 += vf_guided.o framesync.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_HALDCLUT_FILTER)               += vf_lut3d.o framesync.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_HFLIP_FILTER)                  += vf_hflip.o
diff --git a/libavfilter/allfilters.c b/libavfilter/allfilters.c
index 6b9c920..9c60df3 100644
--- a/libavfilter/allfilters.c
+++ b/libavfilter/allfilters.c
@@ -313,6 +313,7 @@ extern const FFFilter ff_vf_gradfun;
 extern const FFFilter ff_vf_graphmonitor;
 extern const FFFilter ff_vf_grayworld;
 extern const FFFilter ff_vf_greyedge;
+extern const FFFilter ff_vf_gsc_v4l2m2m;
 extern const FFFilter ff_vf_guided;
 extern const FFFilter ff_vf_haldclut;
 extern const FFFilter ff_vf_hflip;
diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_gsc_v4l2m2m.c b/libavfilter/vf_gsc_v4l2m2m.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6f4ffd2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_gsc_v4l2m2m.c
@@ -0,0 +1,862 @@
+/*
+ * V4L2 mem2mem colour converter filter (Samsung Exynos GScaler)
+ *
+ * The Exynos display mixer only scans out RGB planes, so YUV frames from
+ * the MFC decoder cannot be put on a plane directly. The GScaler is a
+ * V4L2 mem2mem colour converter: it imports the DRM PRIME frames as
+ * dmabufs and writes XRGB8888 frames that can be scanned out (or imported
+ * by the GPU) without any CPU copy.
+ *
+ * Based on the idea of the decoder->converter pipeline by memeka
+ * (https://github.com/mihailescu2m/FFmpeg/commits/v4l2-drmprime) and on
+ * the structure of the deinterlace_v4l2m2m filter.
+ *
